 "text": "Hello, how are things going? Of course. Are you looking for restaurants that welcome them, or easy at-home tricks? Some gluten free restaurants mark it on the menu, or you can ask at beginning. At home, key is checking ingredients. Wheat, bulgur, barley, rye, pretty much everything. Gluten free cooking uses rice noodles or couscous instead. Then use it sparingly, like a finishing drizzle, rather than soak the noodles. There are gluten free soy sauces now. What else does your roommate like to eat? Not anymore. Gluten free sushi rolls are quite good, and there are already quite a few gluten free ingredients in the mix.",
